      "engram:validUntil": "2026-10-21",
      "prov:hadPrimarySource": {
        "@id": "https://octant.substack.com/p/epoch-13-the-privacy-round"
      },
      "engram:claimClass": "documented",
      "prov:value": "Octant (Golem Foundation) Epoch 13 \"The Privacy Round\", verified 2026-08-12: 100 ETH quadratic-funding matching pool; applications close 2026-09-10; Epoch Accelerator 2026-10-06\u219210-10; allocation window 2026-10-14\u219210-21; apply at https://octant.fillout.com/epoch-13; KYC/KYB mandatory before funding; no geographic/entity restriction so a Swiss non-profit is not blocked. Two categories: Ethereum (private transfers, shielded pools, wallet/RPC privacy, encrypted mempools, ZK tooling) and Open Internet (secure messaging, metadata-protecting communication, private compute hardware, privacy libraries). CRITICAL for Swarm: criterion 2 requires \"privacy is a core property of the project\" \u2014 this DISQUALIFIES a whole-Swarm application, since Swarm is storage/availability first and privacy is a component property. The only credible route is component-level: PSS (maps to \"metadata-protecting communication tools\") and ACT (maps to \"privacy libraries\") \u2014 but criterion 5 requires \"working software with verifiable users\", so PSS/ACT maintenance status and actual users MUST be verified before applying. Quadratic funding rewards breadth of small-donor support, so the effort is community mobilisation during the allocation window (DevRel/marketing work), NOT proposal writing \u2014 which is why it does not compete with the NLnet 2026-11-03 drafting run. Resolves the previously-flagged \"Octant epoch dates unverified / 90-day cadence inferred\" gap.",
      "prov:wasAttributedTo": {
        "@id": "engram:agent/unidentified"
      }
    },
